    "headline": "Nasdaq posts its worst day since June as Intel and Amazon results revive AI-spending doubts",
    "summary": "The S&P 500 fell 1.8% to 7,580.07, the Nasdaq Composite lost 2.9% to 25,437.00 and the Dow dropped 1.1% to 51,770.31. Intel fell almost 29%, its worst day since 1974, while Amazon slid after its report. October was the Nasdaq's worst month since March 2025.",
    "asOf": "2026-10-30T20:21:00Z",
    "bullets": [
      "S&P 500 closed at 7,580.07, down 140.32 points (-1.8%), its worst day since June; Nasdaq Composite 25,437.00 (-2.9%); Dow 51,770.31 (-1.1%) (Associated Press, 4:21 p.m. ET).",
      "Intel fell almost 29% after a fourth-quarter forecast below analyst expectations, its worst day since 1974 (Associated Press).",
      "For October, the Nasdaq fell 5.3%, its worst month since March 2025 (Investopedia). For the week, the S&P 500 is down 0.6% and the Nasdaq down 2.0% (Associated Press).",
      "The 8:30 a.m. Employment Cost Index rose 0.8% in the third quarter and 3.4% over the year, in line with the 0.8% forecast (Bureau of Labor Statistics).",
      "WTI crude rose above $104 a barrel (+2.4%); gold futures fell 3.7% to about $3,883 an ounce; the 10-year Treasury yield was about 4.93% (Investopedia, afternoon session)."
